The two existing D-179 Python relocation controls in #566 still require proof; their original expected verdicts remain unchanged. This follow-up records a reusable **source subproof**, not a product fix or permission to ignore class/self/request context.

Fixed source **fbc9374dc3bcbfc47f403aec0c36e6b51dd7b86c**, PJU Python 3.11.9, HUMAN_AUTHORIZED_LOCAL_PJU_NOT_EC_POOL. All **3,084 physical source members** were checked against the existing input map `51836ac93ce5670644a050f8e3ced2390d377b63bff4b956cc52741b291f9ee5` before and after. Six calls to the unchanged `pure_imported_calls(..., result_proof=primitive_literal_result)` ran; analyze/CLI/pytest/fixture-program execution counts were all zero.

| Diagnostic input | Existing helper result |
|---|---|
| #358 original closed total() returning78.75 | true |
| #263 original source without app.calc.add implementation | false |
| #263 with explicit closed literal add(a,b) implementation | true |
| #263 caller-frame observer producer | false |
| #263 mutating package initializer | false |
| #358 another closed/pure total() returning0 | true |

The two different total definitions both return true **from the purity helper**; neither repository function was executed. This shows why per-side purity booleans cannot substitute for matching side-bound producer identity/value obligations. The stage6 analyzer observations still have #263/#358 originals BLOCK/high, while the separate #358 no-gate control passes; this follow-up does not change those outcomes.

Necessary implementation obligations from independent source review:

1. Resolve BASE and HEAD independently, including diff before/after, package/module ambiguity and all initializer reads. Bind callee/initializer digests and the actual import binding into each side's proof; HEAD cannot stand in for BASE.
2. Prove reaching bindings and cover all relevant calls. `imported_from` alone collects imports without rejecting later rebinding, local shadows or monkeypatches; an empty/missing call list must not become vacuous proof.
3. Validate complete arity/keyword/default/concrete-argument binding. The primitive helper checks literal arguments plus the module grammar; it does not itself reject wrong arity, unknown keyword names or all argument collisions. Unknown fixture/self/custom receiver inputs remain unknown.
4. Preserve independent framework/bootstrap and per-unit execution proof: #263's class construction, pytest alias/mark factory, receiver and startup; #358's function-scoped request identity, OwnMarks, fixture reachability and absence of effects. Producer purity cannot remove those obligations.
5. Preserve full declaration/assertion context, liveness, once-only credit spending and freeze behavior. No blanket context erasure, finite observer-name denylist, altered expected label, severity/strength/alignment change or new exemption follows.

The existing classic-raises consumers show examples of combining narrow purity with stricter context/snapshot and pytest-authority checks; the helper itself is not that full certificate. Build the missing proof path outside the sealed fbc checkout, retain red/current observations, add independent adversarial controls, and qualify a separate sealed source before proposing integration. No implementation or release acceptance is claimed here. The existing #567/#568/#570 dispositions and pre-1.0 human decision remain.

The complete owned driver and its exact observed JSON are retained below so this new evidence is remotely preserved before the workstation shutdown. The driver only parses fixture bytes and calls the unchanged Python helper; it never executes the represented repository programs.

